{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1076,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ezek.15","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Ezekiel","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Ezekiel 15","reference":"Ezekiel 15","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"God by the similitude of a vine, foreshews the utter destruction of Jerusalem, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1-8."},{"verse":3,"text":"2.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":4,"text":"The vine-tree - Israel is here compared to a vine, which, when fruitless, is utterly unprofitable.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":5,"text":"This the prophet minds them of to humble them, and awaken them to fruitfulness.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":6,"text":"A branch - One branch of a tree in the forest is of more use than the whole vine- tree is, except for its fruit.","scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":7,"text":"3.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":8,"text":"A pin - Will it afford even a pin to drive into a wall or post, on which you may safely fasten any weight.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":9,"text":"4.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":10,"text":"For fuel - When for its barrenness it is cut down, it is fit only to burn.","scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":12,"text":"Given - Doomed for food to the fire.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":13,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":14,"text":"Because - They have been so perpetually trespassing, that it seems a continued act.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":15}}